      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer directly in the wiki.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub never holds the Anthropic API key in its own process environment**. Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of the spawned child process** (Ingest agent or Query agent) immediately before that process starts\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is **never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis architecture ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.",
